"""
foamBC - Browse, search, generate and check OpenFOAM boundary conditions.

The database is built by parsing the doxygen header comments
(Description / Usage / \\verbatim / \\table sections) of every class that is
registered as a finite-volume (fvPatchField) or point (pointPatchField)
boundary condition, plus the boundaryField entries of the 0/ files found in
the tutorials (which types are used for which fields and patch roles).

Sub-commands:
    build     Scan the sources and write the database
    list      List boundary conditions (by group, tag or value type)
    search    Full-text search in names and descriptions (English/Japanese)
    show      Show description, example, parameters and tutorial usage
    example   Print real patch entries taken from the tutorials
    typical   Most common types for a field per patch role (from tutorials)
    add       Generate one patch entry (print, or write into 0/<field>)
    recipe    Generate the entries of ALL fields for one patch role
              (velocityInlet, pressureOutlet, wall, ...)
    check     Check the boundaryField of every field file of a case
    html      Generate the stand-alone catalog.html

Database lookup order:
    1. $FOAMBC_DB
    2. ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/foamBC/bcDatabase-<version>.json,
       where <version> is the basename of $WM_PROJECT_DIR (written by 'build')
    3. bcDatabase.json bundled next to this script
"""

